{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And you shall sanctify the breast of the waving and the thigh of the heave-offering, etc.</b> Sanctify them for the generations — that their gift and waving shall apply to the breast and thigh of the shelamim, but not for burning; rather, it shall belong to Aaron and his sons to eat." "<b>Waving.</b> A term of taking out and bringing in; ונטלי״ה בְּלַעַ״ז." "<b>Which is raised up.</b> A term of raising up and bringing down."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French volunteer, 'to wave/elevate' (in liturgical context)"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:36.227628251Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}